// Canonical form of an equation string, for comparing one player's solve with
// another's.
//
// ⚠️ WHAT USED TO LIVE HERE, and why it is gone (2026-09-05). This file was
// `equationOverlap.js` and also held `equationOverlap` and `rankEquations` —
// "how many players solved it the way you did?", answered by grouping on the
// equation STRING alone. That turned out to be wrong: with a value duplicated
// across a white die and a power die, one string is two genuinely different
// solves, and the board rendered one player's dice as everyone's (docs/bugs.md,
// 2026-09-04). The Equations tab now groups on equation + solveColorSignature
// and does it itself, which left both functions with no production caller.
//
// `normalizeEquation` survives because that grouping still needs it: ×/*, −/-,
// ÷// and ＋/+ must not split otherwise-identical solves.
//
// ⚠️ There is a SECOND, private `normalizeEquation` in
// equation-engine/equationUtils.js. The two are not verified to agree and are
// deliberately not merged here — that is a correctness question, not a tidy-up,
// and belongs in its own change.

/**
 * Canonical form of an equation string for comparison: strip whitespace and
 * fold display glyphs (× − ÷ ＋) back to ASCII operators.
 * @param {string} eq
 * @returns {string}
 */
export function normalizeEquation(eq) {
  if (!eq) return '';
  return String(eq)
    .replace(/\s+/g, '')
    .replace(/×/g, '*')
    .replace(/÷/g, '/')
    .replace(/−/g, '-')
    .replace(/＋/g, '+');
}
